# Root .gitattributes — LF line endings for every text file
#
# All text files are stored and checked out as LF on every platform, which
# overrides any core.autocrlf setting. Binary files are auto-detected and left
# untouched.
#
# Why: Go test fixtures are compared byte-for-byte or with LF-expecting
# parsers; markdown (design documents, protocol sources) is embedded verbatim
# into deployment transform outputs, which must be deterministic across
# platforms; and agents and Go tooling write LF, so CRLF checkouts made
# untouched files show up as modified.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit rules kept so these files stay LF even if git misdetects them as binary.
*.md text eol=lf
**/testdata/**/*.golden.txt text eol=lf
**/testdata/**/*.sh text eol=lf
